<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Kuban Soviet Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1918 CE · capital Yekaterinodar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Bolshevik republic proclaimed in the Kuban in spring 1918, contested by the Kuban Cossack government and the Volunteer Army.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In March 1918 Red forces took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuban-rada">Kuban Rada</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> regional government, which fled. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Bolsheviks</a> proclaimed the Kuban Soviet Republic in April 1918 as an autonomous part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a>, governing the Kuban region and its large Cossack and non-Cossack peasant population.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The republic was run by a council of commissars and relied on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-guards-russia">Red Guard</a> units and non-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> settlers, who resented Cossack privileges in land. It repelled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lavr-kornilov">Kornilov</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a> in April 1918, where Kornilov was killed. Grain requisitioning and conflict with the Cossacks undermined its support.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In May 1918 it merged with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/black-sea-soviet-republic">Black Sea Soviet Republic</a> to form the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kuban-black-sea-soviet-republic">Kuban-Black Sea Soviet Republic</a>, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-movement">Whites</a> overran later that year. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krasnodar">Yekaterinodar</a> fell to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volunteer-army">Volunteer Army</a> in August 1918.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kuban-soviet-republic.jpg" alt="Kuban Soviet Republic" width="320" height="224"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Wassily assumed (based on copyright claims). · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9A%D1%83%D0%B1%D0%B0%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%8F_%D0%BE%D0%B1%D0%BB%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%82%D1%8C_1900.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Yekaterinodar</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kuban SR</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=kuban-soviet-republic" aria-label="Kuban Soviet Republic on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5607 587 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kuban Soviet Republic lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5927 843L5820 533M5927 843L5927 843"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5820 533h0M5927 843h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5927 843h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5927 843h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1918&amp;focus=kuban-soviet-republic">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
